v {xschem version=3.4.4 file_version=1.2}
G {}
K {type=subcircuit
format="@name @pinlist @symname"
template="name=x1"
description="The sky130-trng entropy source: two separately-supplied 11-stage starved rings, XOR-combined into xo. Array size and stage count are PROVISIONAL placeholders pending the sky130 jitter characterization named in spec/porting-plan.md section 2.2 -- see ro_array_core.sch. Pin order MUST track design/xschem/ro_array_core.sch's own .subckt signature exactly: en1 en2 vddr1 vddr2 vdd vss xo ro1 ro2 -- see design/ro_array_core.spice. ro1/ro2 are OBSERVATION-ONLY outputs so a per-ring liveness digitizer in sampler_core.sch can reach each ring node; they add no device and change no ring, and a parent that leaves them unconnected gets exactly the circuit this cell had before they existed. They are not a raw tap and never leave the die."
}
